Per-launch fresh candidate-writable state in the measurement phase

Each loader launch now runs against a per-launch transpiler cache and
TMPDIR under a root-owned measurement root, inside a fresh IPC namespace,
and is followed by a candidate-uid process reap (subreaper-backed) and a
purge of the shared tmp roots; the post-test lockdown rebuilds the 0777
build/test scratch dirs root-owned and strips group/other write from
root-owned paths under the build tree, so no repetition can replay
resolution state persisted by an earlier one.
